\section{Installation and Package Structure}
\label{sec:install}
%% ============================================================

\subsection{Installation}

\texttt{perm\_pateda} depends on \texttt{pateda}.  Since \texttt{pateda} is an
in-development package, install it first from the local checkout and then install
\texttt{perm\_pateda}:

\begin{lstlisting}[language=bash]
pip3 install -e packages/pateda
pip3 install -e packages/perm_pateda
\end{lstlisting}

\noindent For the development tooling (\texttt{pytest}, \texttt{ruff},
\texttt{black}, \texttt{mypy}):

\begin{lstlisting}[language=bash]
pip3 install -e "packages/perm_pateda[dev]"
\end{lstlisting}

Required dependencies are \texttt{numpy}, \texttt{scipy} and \texttt{pateda}.
The mixture of Plackett--Luce models additionally uses
\texttt{scikit-learn} ($k$-means in the spectral initialization), and the
statistical utilities use \texttt{pandas} and \texttt{matplotlib}.  Python
$\geq 3.9$ is required.

\subsection{Package Structure}

The top-level \texttt{perm\_pateda} namespace exposes the algorithm classes, the
distances, the consensus estimators, the random-key conversion helpers, the
benchmark readers and the statistical utilities:

